{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally Comes Home"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Scrapbooking"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le14ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past Tense and Past Continuous tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished. </br>You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular. </p> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span>.</p> Irregular verbs change in different ways. </p>For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">did</span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask\u2026?</span> </p><span class=\"strong\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"strong\">to do</span>.</p> For Past Continuous, we add <span class=\"strong\">was/were</span> + verb\u201c<span class=\"strong\">ing</span>\u201d to verbs.</p> Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add \u201c<span class=\"strong\">ing</span>\u201d."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were talking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"count\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"counted\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were counting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were going\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"take\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"took\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were taking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"travel\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"traveled\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were traveling\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"buy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were buying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were thinking\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was going through some pictures on my camera and I printed some out."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We were watching a group of gazelles when a rhino came out of nowhere!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "scrapbook"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a book of blank pages for sticking clippings and pictures in"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I make a scrapbook after each trip I take."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about photo albums."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "album"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a blank book for keeping pictures or photos "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love old photo albums."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "That's quite something!"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "That's very impressive!"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love the picture of the rhino running! That's quite something!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to count sheep"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to close your eyes and count to help you fall asleep"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I was counting sheep until 2 a.m. last night when I finally fell asleep!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go through"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to search through or examine in sequence"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was going through the pictures on my camera and I printed some out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "out of nowhere"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "by surprise; suddenly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The rhino appeared out of nowhere!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le14ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a short paragraph (8-10 lines) about a favorite memory."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe when it was, where it took place and how old you were."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use comparatives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Simple Past and Past Continuous tenses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your paragraph to your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about what I was doing when something else happened."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write 8 -10 lines about my favorite memory."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare things and feelings."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le14ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le14ob05re2img06.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le14ob05re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: How's the jetlag this morning, Sally? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It's getting there ... I was counting sheep until 2 a.m. last night when I finally fell asleep!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: You used to do that all the time when you were little!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: That's true, but I wasn't traveling the world as a kid. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Well, you had lots of fun in Cambridge anyway. What are these?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Oh, I was going through the pictures on my camera and I printed some out.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le14ob05re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: What do you want to do with them?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I was thinking of making a scrapbook about my trip.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Great idea! I made scrapbooks all the time when I was your age.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I think you showed them to me! I love the old photo albums too!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Anyway, I want to hear about your travel adventures!", "